        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.92,
          "end": 47.73,
          "en": "So after on calculate investment results executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.73,
          "end": 50.28,
          "en": "this results data property is changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.28,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "And this method here will be triggered when the user clicks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "to calculate button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.47,
          "en": "So put number words, this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.47,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "Results data is some stateful data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 65.76,
          "en": "some data which when changed will have an impact on the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 69.06,
          "en": "And that's some data we could manage with a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 71.103,
          "en": "instead of using it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.3,
          "end": 73.44,
          "en": "How would we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "Well, as a first step, I'll get rid of that type annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "and that question mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "And I'll instead initialize results data as a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 87.82,
          "en": "by assigning a Signal value by executing the signal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.74,
          "end": 92.88300000000001,
          "en": "and the Signal function is imported from Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 99.27000000000001,
          "en": "Now this Signal then also needs an initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "and that initial value could be undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "that would be fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "but eventually I wanna store a different value in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 112.74000000000001,
          "en": "So I'll add angle brackets to add this type annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.74000000000001,
          "end": 117.74000000000001,
          "en": "to tell Signal which kind of value it will eventually store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 123.36,
          "en": "And I'll then grab this results type definition again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.36,
          "end": 127.48,
          "en": "this array full of object types that have this shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "and add that here between the angle brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 138.45,
          "en": "Now undefined is now actually not a valid value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.45,
          "end": 142.75,
          "en": "if we tell Angular that this is the expected type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "and therefore we need to clarify this type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "here by adding the pipe symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "and then adding undefined thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 156.99,
          "en": "This is TypeScript way of defining two possible types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.99,
          "end": 158.913,
          "en": "for a given value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.5,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "So with that, we're telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "that this Signal will hold either an array full of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 170.94299999999998,
          "en": "that have this shape or an undefined value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 173.91,
          "end": 176.91,
          "en": "So that would be one way of working with signals here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 176.91,
          "end": 178.173,
          "en": "and of setting this up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 181.53,
          "en": "Now we also need to change the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "where we update the results data though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "because this line of code won't work anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "Instead, since results data now is a Signal, we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 191.88,
          "en": "to call this set method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 195.183,
          "en": "and set it to this annual data as a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.04,
          "end": 198.57,
          "en": "But that's then it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.57,
          "end": 202.803,
          "en": "That's how we migrate this code here to use signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 205.8,
          "en": "It's not all we have to do though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.8,
          "end": 209.43,
          "en": "We also need to work on the app component template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 212.01,
          "en": "because there I'm passing my results data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.01,
          "end": 214.71,
          "en": "to the results property of the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 216.93,
          "en": "investment results component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 216.93,
          "end": 220.38,
          "en": "and results of course doesn't want a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.38,
          "end": 223.173,
          "en": "it wants the data inside the Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 226.59,
          "en": "So we need to read the Signal data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.59,
          "end": 230.49,
          "en": "and let Angular set up a subscription behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 232.023,
          "en": "by adding brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.69,
          "end": 237.87,
          "en": "That's all though with that if you save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237.87,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "and you enter some valid data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 241.44,
          "end": 243.45,
          "en": "this should work as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.45,
          "end": 245.313,
          "en": "But now using a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 247.2,
          "end": 250.53,
          "en": "it's not the only place where we can use a Signal though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.53,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "Instead, the user input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 256.17,
          "en": "actually also has some properties that change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 256.17,
          "end": 258.87,
          "en": "as the user enters some new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 261.09,
          "en": "with help of two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 261.09,
          "end": 264.39,
          "en": "And we can also use signals here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 264.39,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "So we can turn all these properties into signals by calling",
